WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.283 --> 00:00:02.937
- [Narrator] It's November 6th, 1814.

00:00:02.937 --> 00:00:04.785
In the Belgian city of Dinant,
in a modest house built

00:00:04.785 --> 00:00:06.147
on a street that would
later bear his name,

00:00:06.147 --> 00:00:06.980
- [Adolphe Voiceover] Hello.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.563
- [Narrator] Adolphe Sax was born.

00:00:08.563 --> 00:00:10.578
28 years later while living in Paris,

00:00:10.578 --> 00:00:12.818
Sax would invent the saxophone
and revolutionize music

00:00:12.818 --> 00:00:14.953
in ways he couldn't imagine.

00:00:14.953 --> 00:00:17.256
But this isn't that
story, this is the story

00:00:17.256 --> 00:00:19.437
of how Adolphe Sax
escaped death seven times

00:00:19.437 --> 00:00:22.020
before inventing the saxophone.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:26.249
Hardly old enough to
stand, the young Adolphe

00:00:26.249 --> 00:00:28.380
fell down three flights of stairs.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.635
A stone floor broke his fall.

00:00:30.635 --> 00:00:32.228
At the age of three, Adolphe swallowed

00:00:32.228 --> 00:00:34.409
a bowl of watered-down sulphuric acid,

00:00:34.409 --> 00:00:36.095
mistaking it for milk.

00:00:36.095 --> 00:00:37.358
Years later, Adolphe found himself

00:00:37.358 --> 00:00:40.860
a bit too close to a gunpowder explosion.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.981
He was again burned when
a cast iron frying pan

00:00:42.981 --> 00:00:44.784
was not knocked over onto him.

00:00:44.784 --> 00:00:46.423
Later, a roof stone fell on his head,

00:00:46.423 --> 00:00:48.857
leaving a life-long scar.

00:00:48.857 --> 00:00:50.822
Adolphe was nearly asphyxiated
when recently varnished

00:00:50.822 --> 00:00:52.947
items were left in his bedroom overnight.

00:00:52.947 --> 00:00:54.530
He woke up, barely.

00:00:55.649 --> 00:00:57.193
Playing with friends in a nearby river,

00:00:57.193 --> 00:01:00.079
Adolphe was swept up in a swift
current and nearly drowned.

00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:01.662
Again, he survived.

00:01:07.001 --> 00:01:11.330
On February 7th, 1894, Adolphe
died peacefully in Paris.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:13.054
The saxophone had already
crossed the Atlantic,

00:01:13.054 --> 00:01:15.316
prime to evolve into an
icon of American jazz music

00:01:15.316 --> 00:01:18.065
and guaranteeing Sax his immortality.

00:01:18.065 --> 00:01:21.398
(jazz background music)

